  {
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "256da135-1d70-5bab-a433-10f87b39cba4",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} - \\frac{2 y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} - \\frac{2 y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =- 2 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =- 2 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{3 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fae37f8a-4da0-5e6d-b431-1bcddc784e5e",
