      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
